<section id="Ax1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix">Appendix</h2>

</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Two Point Deterministic Equivalent for General Free Product From Dynamical Mean Field Theory</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we describe a method to handle two-point correlation properties of free products of random matrices. Similar results were provided in a simple random feature model of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bordelon et al., 2024a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Atanasov et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. This computation provides the necessary technical results to establish the behavior of ICL in the randomly rotated context setting. Note throughout that we will use <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{tr}\bm{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{tr}\bm{M}</annotation></semantics></math> for normalized trace of the matrix <math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}</annotation></semantics></math> so that for <math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\times N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\times N</annotation></semantics></math> matrix <math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{tr}\bm{M}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}M_{kk}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{tr}\bm{M}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{k=1}^{N}M_{kk}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tracking Linear Dynamics Generated by Free Product</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Taking a dynamical approach, we consider the following dynamical system which depends on a random matrix <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times N}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A1.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{t}\bm{v}(t)=-\bm{M}\bm{v}(t)+\delta(t)\bm{v}_{0}\ ,\ \bm{M}=\bm{O}\bm{B}\bm{O}^{\top}\bm{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑶</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{t}\bm{v}(t)=-\bm{M}\bm{v}(t)+\delta(t)\bm{v}_{0}\ ,\ \bm{M}=\bm{O}\bm{B}\bm{O}^{\top}\bm{A}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{O}</annotation></semantics></math> is a random <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\times N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\times N</annotation></semantics></math> orthogonal matrix drawn from the Haar measure for the orthogonal group. Our starting point is to express the above dynamical system with an integral representation of Dirac-Delta functions <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1=\int dz\delta(z)=\int\frac{dzd\chi}{2\pi i}e^{-\chi z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1=\int dz\delta(z)=\int\frac{dzd\chi}{2\pi i}e^{-\chi z}</annotation></semantics></math> where the integration variable <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi\in(-i\infty,i\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi\in(-i\infty,i\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> runs along the imaginary axis. Performing this for each time <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> of the dynamics yields</p>
<table id="A1.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle Z=\int\mathcal{D}\bm{v}\mathcal{D}\bm{\chi}\left&lt;\exp\left(-\int dt\bm{\chi}(t)\left[\partial_{t}\bm{v}(t)+\bm{M}\bm{v}(t)-\bm{v}_{0}\delta(t)\right]\right)\right&gt;=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>𝒗</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>𝝌</mi><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>𝝌</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>𝒗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z=\int\mathcal{D}\bm{v}\mathcal{D}\bm{\chi}\left&lt;\exp\left(-\int dt\bm{\chi}(t)\left[\partial_{t}\bm{v}(t)+\bm{M}\bm{v}(t)-\bm{v}_{0}\delta(t)\right]\right)\right&gt;=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}\bm{v}\mathcal{D}\bm{\chi}=\lim_{\delta t\to 0}\prod_{n=-\infty}^{\infty}\frac{d\bm{v}(n\cdot\delta t)d\bm{\chi}(n\cdot\delta t)}{2\pi i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝌</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">lim</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}\bm{v}\mathcal{D}\bm{\chi}=\lim_{\delta t\to 0}\prod_{n=-\infty}^{\infty}\frac{d\bm{v}(n\cdot\delta t)d\bm{\chi}(n\cdot\delta t)}{2\pi i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the flat measure over <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}(t),\bm{\chi}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝝌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}(t),\bm{\chi}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> in the continuous time limit <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta t\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta t\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. The average <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left&lt;\cdot\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left&lt;\cdot\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> is computed over the random orthogonal matrix <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{O}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To simplify the calculation, we transform our dynamics into Fourier space</p>
<table id="A1.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{v}(t)\equiv\int\frac{d\omega}{2\pi}\exp\left(i\omega t\right)\bm{v}(\omega)\ ,\ \bm{\chi}(t)\equiv\int\frac{d\omega}{2\pi}\exp\left(i\omega t\right)\bm{\chi}(\omega)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{v}(t)\equiv\int\frac{d\omega}{2\pi}\exp\left(i\omega t\right)\bm{v}(\omega)\ ,\ \bm{\chi}(t)\equiv\int\frac{d\omega}{2\pi}\exp\left(i\omega t\right)\bm{\chi}(\omega),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">which transforms the original integral over <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> into an integral over <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int d\omega\bm{\chi}(\omega)\cdot[(i\omega)\bm{v}(\omega)+\bm{M}\bm{v}(\omega)-\bm{v}_{0}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int d\omega\bm{\chi}(\omega)\cdot[(i\omega)\bm{v}(\omega)+\bm{M}\bm{v}(\omega)-\bm{v}_{0}]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Disorder Average</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Averaging the resulting expression over the orthogonal matrix <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{O}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the following representation of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> as an integral over order parameters <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{\Sigma},\bm{\Psi}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{\Sigma},\bm{\Psi}\}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A1.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z=\int\mathcal{D}\bm{\Sigma}\mathcal{D}\bm{\Psi}\exp\left(-N\mathcal{S}[\bm{\Sigma},\bm{\Psi}]\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z=\int\mathcal{D}\bm{\Sigma}\mathcal{D}\bm{\Psi}\exp\left(-N\mathcal{S}[\bm{\Sigma},\bm{\Psi}]\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In the above expression, the action <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math> has the form</p>
<table id="A1.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E27.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{S}[\bm{\Sigma},\bm{\Psi}]=-\text{Tr}\bm{\Sigma}\bm{\Psi}-\frac{1}{N}\ln\mathcal{Z}_{A}(\bm{\Psi})-\text{Tr}\bm{\Sigma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star}-\frac{1}{N}\ln\det\left(\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star}\otimes\bm{I}+\bm{V}\otimes\bm{B}\right)+\ln\det\bm{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>𝚿</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ln</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mtext>Tr</mtext><mi>𝚺</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ln</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{S}[\bm{\Sigma},\bm{\Psi}]=-\text{Tr}\bm{\Sigma}\bm{\Psi}-\frac{1}{N}\ln\mathcal{Z}_{A}(\bm{\Psi})-\text{Tr}\bm{\Sigma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star}-\frac{1}{N}\ln\det\left(\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star}\otimes\bm{I}+\bm{V}\otimes\bm{B}\right)+\ln\det\bm{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> solves the implicit equation <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\mathcal{S}}{\partial\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star}}=-\bm{\Sigma}+\text{tr}\left(\bm{\hat{\Sigma}}_{\star}\otimes\bm{I}+\bm{V}\otimes\bm{B}\right)^{-1}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\mathcal{S}}{\partial\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star}}=-\bm{\Sigma}+\text{tr}\left(\bm{\hat{\Sigma}}_{\star}\otimes\bm{I}+\bm{V}\otimes\bm{B}\right)^{-1}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and the single site measure <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math> has the form</p>
<table id="A1.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{Z}_{A}(\bm{\Psi})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{Z}_{A}(\bm{\Psi})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\mathcal{D}\bm{v}\mathcal{D}\bm{\chi}\exp\left(-\int d\omega\bm{\chi}(\omega)\cdot\left[(i\omega)\bm{v}(z)-\bm{v}_{0}-\int d\omega^{\prime}\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\bm{v}(\omega^{\prime})\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>𝒗</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>𝝌</mi><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>𝝌</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>𝒗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\mathcal{D}\bm{v}\mathcal{D}\bm{\chi}\exp\left(-\int d\omega\bm{\chi}(\omega)\cdot\left[(i\omega)\bm{v}(z)-\bm{v}_{0}-\int d\omega^{\prime}\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\bm{v}(\omega^{\prime})\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E28.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}\int d\omega d\omega^{\prime}\left[\Psi_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\bm{v}(\omega)^{\top}\bm{A}^{2}\bm{v}(\omega^{\prime})+\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\bm{\chi}(\omega)\cdot\bm{\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\right]\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>ω</mi><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝝌</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝝌</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\left(-\frac{1}{2}\int d\omega d\omega^{\prime}\left[\Psi_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\bm{v}(\omega)^{\top}\bm{A}^{2}\bm{v}(\omega^{\prime})+\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\bm{\chi}(\omega)\cdot\bm{\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\right]\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Taking the Large System Size Limit</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To study the limit of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, the saddle point equations over <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math> give</p>
<table id="A1.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{S}}{\partial\bm{\Psi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})}=-\begin{bmatrix}\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\\
\Sigma_{\chi v}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;\Sigma_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{N}\left&lt;\bm{v}(\omega)^{\top}\bm{A}^{2}\bm{v}(\omega^{\prime})\right&gt;&amp;\frac{1}{N}\left&lt;\bm{v}(\omega)^{\top}\bm{A}\bm{\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\right&gt;\\
\frac{1}{N}\left&lt;\bm{\chi}(\omega)^{\top}\bm{A}\bm{v}(\omega^{\prime})\right&gt;&amp;\frac{1}{N}\left&lt;\bm{\chi}(\omega)\cdot\bm{\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\right&gt;\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝝌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>𝝌</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{S}}{\partial\bm{\Psi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})}=-\begin{bmatrix}\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\\
\Sigma_{\chi v}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;\Sigma_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\end{bmatrix}+\begin{bmatrix}\frac{1}{N}\left&lt;\bm{v}(\omega)^{\top}\bm{A}^{2}\bm{v}(\omega^{\prime})\right&gt;&amp;\frac{1}{N}\left&lt;\bm{v}(\omega)^{\top}\bm{A}\bm{\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\right&gt;\\
\frac{1}{N}\left&lt;\bm{\chi}(\omega)^{\top}\bm{A}\bm{v}(\omega^{\prime})\right&gt;&amp;\frac{1}{N}\left&lt;\bm{\chi}(\omega)\cdot\bm{\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\right&gt;\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{S}}{\partial\bm{\Sigma}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})}=-\bm{\Psi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})-\bm{\hat{\Sigma}}_{\star}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})+[\bm{\Sigma}^{-1}](\omega,\omega^{\prime})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{S}}{\partial\bm{\Sigma}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})}=-\bm{\Psi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})-\bm{\hat{\Sigma}}_{\star}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})+[\bm{\Sigma}^{-1}](\omega,\omega^{\prime})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The average over <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left&lt;\cdot\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left&lt;\cdot\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> represents an average over the Gaussian measure defined by <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Z}_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒵</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Z}_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>. The solution to these equations has the following block structure</p>
<table id="A1.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Sigma}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=\begin{bmatrix}\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\\
\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;0\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Sigma}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=\begin{bmatrix}\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\\
\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;0\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\\
\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;\hat{\Sigma}_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\\
\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;\hat{\Sigma}_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Psi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\\
\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\end{bmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚿</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Psi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=\begin{bmatrix}0&amp;\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\\
\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})&amp;\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\end{bmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Off Diagonal Blocks</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The off diagonal blocks decouple over different frequencies <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=\delta(\omega-\omega^{\prime})\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=\delta(\omega-\omega^{\prime})\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> and satisfy the following equations</p>
<table id="A1.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)=\text{tr}\bm{A}\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}=\text{tr}\left(\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega)+\bm{B}\right)^{-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)=\text{tr}\bm{A}\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}=\text{tr}\left(\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega)+\bm{B}\right)^{-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)=1-\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega)\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)=1-\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega)\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Introduce the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-transform <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{M}</annotation></semantics></math> of a matrix <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A1.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau_{M}(i\omega)\equiv\text{tr}\bm{M}(i\omega+\bm{M})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau_{M}(i\omega)\equiv\text{tr}\bm{M}(i\omega+\bm{M})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">as well as its inverse function <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\omega_{M}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\omega_{M}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            Up to a change in signs and <math id="footnote2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\omega\to-z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\omega\to-z</annotation></semantics></math> this is equivalent to the <math id="footnote2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-transform of a random matrix <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Potters &amp; Bouchaud, 2020</a>)</cite>.</span></span></span>. Then our saddle point equations give us</p>
<table id="A1.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau=\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)=\tau_{A}(i\omega_{A})=\tau_{B}(i\omega_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau=\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)=\tau_{A}(i\omega_{A})=\tau_{B}(i\omega_{B})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\omega_{A}=\frac{i\omega}{\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\omega_{A}=\frac{i\omega}{\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\omega_{B}=(\tau^{-1}-1)\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>B</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\omega_{B}=(\tau^{-1}-1)\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>. Putting these equations together, we find</p>
<table id="A1.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(i\omega_{A}(\tau))(i\omega_{B}(\tau))=\frac{1-\tau}{\tau}(i\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(i\omega_{A}(\tau))(i\omega_{B}(\tau))=\frac{1-\tau}{\tau}(i\omega)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">This equation is to be solved for <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math>. Once this function is determined we can use it to compute the diagonal blocks of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma},\bm{\Psi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚿</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma},\bm{\Psi}</annotation></semantics></math> as we describe in the next section.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Diagonal Blocks</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now, we can determine the diagonal blocks, which determine the covariance structure of the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> variables</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A1.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\bm{v}_{0}^{\top}\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\bm{A}^{2}\left(i\omega^{\prime}+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\bm{v}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{N}\bm{v}_{0}^{\top}\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\bm{A}^{2}\left(i\omega^{\prime}+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\bm{v}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\ \underbrace{\text{tr}\bm{A}^{2}\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\left(i\omega^{\prime}+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\right)^{-1}}_{\mathcal{A}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\ \underbrace{\text{tr}\bm{A}^{2}\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\left(i\omega^{\prime}+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\right)^{-1}}_{\mathcal{A}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\hat{\Sigma}_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\ \underbrace{\text{tr}\left(\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega)+\bm{B}\right)^{-1}\left(\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})+\bm{B}\right)^{-1}}_{\mathcal{B}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑩</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\hat{\Sigma}_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\ \underbrace{\text{tr}\left(\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega)+\bm{B}\right)^{-1}\left(\hat{\Sigma}_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})+\bm{B}\right)^{-1}}_{\mathcal{B}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\hat{\Sigma}_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})-\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)^{-1}\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\hat{\Sigma}_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})-\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)^{-1}\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where we introduced functions <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math> which can be determined from the (already obtained) off-diagonal blocks. Combining these equations</p>
<table id="A1.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E39.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\frac{1}{N}\bm{v}_{0}^{\top}\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\bm{A}^{2}\left(i\omega^{\prime}+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\bm{v}_{0}}{1-\left[\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)^{-1}\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})^{-1}-\mathcal{B}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})^{-1}\right]\mathcal{A}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\frac{1}{N}\bm{v}_{0}^{\top}\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\bm{A}^{2}\left(i\omega^{\prime}+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\bm{v}_{0}}{1-\left[\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)^{-1}\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})^{-1}-\mathcal{B}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})^{-1}\right]\mathcal{A}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.2" class="ltx_p">From this expression, both <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\Sigma}_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=-\mathcal{B}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\Sigma}_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=-\mathcal{B}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=-\hat{\Sigma}_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})-\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)^{-1}\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})=-\hat{\Sigma}_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})-\Sigma_{vv}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega)^{-1}\Sigma_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> are determined.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Deterministic Equivalent</h5>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the functions <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> we obtain the following determinstic equivalent for the outer product of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}</annotation></semantics></math> variables</p>
<table id="A1.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{v}(\omega)\bm{v}(\omega^{\prime})^{\top}\simeq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>≃</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{v}(\omega)\bm{v}(\omega^{\prime})^{\top}\simeq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\left[\bm{v}_{0}\bm{v}_{0}-\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\bm{I}\right]\left(i\omega^{\prime}+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\right)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\left[\bm{v}_{0}\bm{v}_{0}-\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\bm{I}\right]\left(i\omega^{\prime}+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\simeq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≃</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\simeq</annotation></semantics></math> expression holds under trace against a test matrix (i.e. <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}_{1}\simeq\bm{M}_{2}\implies\text{tr}\bm{C}\bm{M}_{1}=\text{tr}\bm{C}\bm{M}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≃</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑴</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}_{1}\simeq\bm{M}_{2}\implies\text{tr}\bm{C}\bm{M}_{1}=\text{tr}\bm{C}\bm{M}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Potters &amp; Bouchaud, 2020</a>)</cite>. This function will be used in subsequent expressions to give an exact result for the loss landscape of our randomly rotated ICL loss function. Approximations of this will give rise to our scaling law results as we discuss in Appendix <a href="#A6.SS4" title="F.4 Orthogonal projection and A is Structured Wishart ‣ Appendix F Scaling Law Theory ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.4</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Model Definition, Masking Mechanics, Reduced-<math id="A2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> Model</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Linear Attention and Positional Masking For our Task</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide more detail on the structure of the masking used in our task. First, we note that the target values <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> are only provided for the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> labeled examples within each context matrix. Second, we note that the residual attention operations are masked differently for the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> labeled examples and the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> evaluation points. To define our masking operation precisely, we introduce the notation <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{1}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{1}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> as a vector consisting of all <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> entries equal to one. We introduce the masking matrix <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}\in\mathbb{R}^{(P+K)\times(P+K)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}\in\mathbb{R}^{(P+K)\times(P+K)}</annotation></semantics></math> for the residual stream which has the following block structure</p>
<table id="A2.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{M}=\begin{bmatrix}-\bm{1}_{P}\ \bm{1}_{P}^{\top}&amp;\bm{0}\\
\bm{1}_{K}\ \bm{1}_{P}^{\top}&amp;\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mn class="ltx_mathvariant_bold" mathvariant="bold"> 1</mn><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{M}=\begin{bmatrix}-\bm{1}_{P}\ \bm{1}_{P}^{\top}&amp;\bm{0}\\
\bm{1}_{K}\ \bm{1}_{P}^{\top}&amp;\bm{0}\end{bmatrix}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Now that this positional masking matrix is introduced, we can conveniently express our update rule for the residual stream</p>
<table id="A2.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{h}^{\ell+1}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{h}^{\ell+1}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{h}^{\ell}_{\mu}+\frac{1}{PL}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P+K}M_{\mu\nu}\left(\bm{k}^{\ell}_{\nu}\cdot\bm{q}^{\ell}_{\mu}\right)\bm{v}_{\nu}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{h}^{\ell}_{\mu}+\frac{1}{PL}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P+K}M_{\mu\nu}\left(\bm{k}^{\ell}_{\nu}\cdot\bm{q}^{\ell}_{\mu}\right)\bm{v}_{\nu}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{h}^{\ell}_{\mu}+\frac{1}{PL}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}M_{\mu\nu}\left(\bm{k}^{\ell}_{\nu}\cdot\bm{q}^{\ell}_{\mu}\right)\bm{v}_{\nu}^{\ell}\ ,\ \mu\in[P+K]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>P</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{h}^{\ell}_{\mu}+\frac{1}{PL}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}M_{\mu\nu}\left(\bm{k}^{\ell}_{\nu}\cdot\bm{q}^{\ell}_{\mu}\right)\bm{v}_{\nu}^{\ell}\ ,\ \mu\in[P+K]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{k}^{\ell}_{\mu}=\bm{W}_{k}\cdot\bm{h}^{\ell}_{\mu},\bm{q}^{\ell}_{\mu}=\bm{W}_{q}\bm{h}^{\ell}_{\mu},\bm{v}^{\ell}_{\mu}=\bm{W}^{\ell}_{v}\bm{h}^{\ell}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒌</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒒</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{k}^{\ell}_{\mu}=\bm{W}_{k}\cdot\bm{h}^{\ell}_{\mu},\bm{q}^{\ell}_{\mu}=\bm{W}_{q}\bm{h}^{\ell}_{\mu},\bm{v}^{\ell}_{\mu}=\bm{W}^{\ell}_{v}\bm{h}^{\ell}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and we dropped the sum over evaluation points <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{P+1,...,P+K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{P+1,...,P+K\}</annotation></semantics></math> due to the structure of the positional mask <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}</annotation></semantics></math>. We thus see that the masked update rule has two properties</p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It prevents the test points <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\in\{P+1,...,P+K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\{P+1,...,P+K\}</annotation></semantics></math> from being used in the residual stream updates. Only the first <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> training points are utilized.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It provides an opposite sign for the updates on training points and on testing points. We will see that this will enable the model to implement an in-context gradient descent rule. In such a rule, a subspace of the residual variables will encode residual errors <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\mu}-f_{\mu}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\mu}-f_{\mu}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for the training predictions and <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+f_{\mu}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+f_{\mu}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> for the test points <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mu\in\{P+1,..,P+K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">.</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\in\{P+1,..,P+K\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Instead, one could use the same signs for training points and test points in <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}</annotation></semantics></math> and simply negate the output of the model at the end <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\to-f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\to-f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Derivation of Reduced Gamma Model</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we describe the conditions under which a linear attention transformer model can be reparameterized as the recurrent reduced-<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> model we discuss in the main text.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Alignment Assumptions</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Von Oswald et al. (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib75" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al. (2025)</a></cite>, we study configurations of weights that encode information about inputs <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and targets <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> in orthogonal subspaces of the residual stream. Concretely, the following assumptions are made on the input weights, which implement in-context preconditioned gradient descent</p>
<table id="A2.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{W}_{x}^{\top}\bm{w}_{y}=0\ ,\ \bm{W}_{x}^{\top}\bm{w}_{o}=0\ ,\ \bm{w}_{y}\cdot\bm{w}_{y}=|\bm{w}_{y}||\bm{w}_{y}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>o</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{W}_{x}^{\top}\bm{w}_{y}=0\ ,\ \bm{W}_{x}^{\top}\bm{w}_{o}=0\ ,\ \bm{w}_{y}\cdot\bm{w}_{y}=|\bm{w}_{y}||\bm{w}_{y}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Collectively these assumptions imply that read-in weights for the targets <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{w}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{w}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> and readout weights <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{w}_{o}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{w}_{o}</annotation></semantics></math> perfectly align and that the read-in weights for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒙</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> project input data to an orthgonal subspace. Next we study the following set of alignment conditions for the key, query and value matrices</p>
<table id="A2.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{W}_{x}^{\top}\left(\bm{W}_{k}^{\ell}\right)^{\top}\bm{W}_{q}^{\ell}\bm{W}_{x}\propto\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{W}_{x}^{\top}\left(\bm{W}_{k}^{\ell}\right)^{\top}\bm{W}_{q}^{\ell}\bm{W}_{x}\propto\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{W}_{v}\bm{W}_{x}=0\ ,\ \bm{W}_{v}\bm{w}_{y}\propto\bm{w}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∝</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{W}_{v}\bm{W}_{x}=0\ ,\ \bm{W}_{v}\bm{w}_{y}\propto\bm{w}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Under these assumptions, we can define a collection of <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\times D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\times D</annotation></semantics></math> matrices <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\equiv\left(\bm{w}_{o}^{\top}\bm{W}_{v}^{\ell}\bm{w}_{y}\right)\bm{W}_{x}^{\top}(\bm{W}_{k}^{\ell})^{\top}(\bm{W}_{q}^{\ell})\bm{W}_{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>o</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>q</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\equiv\left(\bm{w}_{o}^{\top}\bm{W}_{v}^{\ell}\bm{w}_{y}\right)\bm{W}_{x}^{\top}(\bm{W}_{k}^{\ell})^{\top}(\bm{W}_{q}^{\ell})\bm{W}_{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which gives rise to the following residual stream dynamics for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mu}^{\ell}\equiv\bm{w}_{o}\cdot\bm{h}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mu}^{\ell}\equiv\bm{w}_{o}\cdot\bm{h}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{\ell+1}_{\mu}=\Delta^{\ell}_{\mu}+\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}M_{\mu\nu}\bm{x}_{\nu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\bm{x}_{\mu}\Delta_{\nu}^{\ell}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>P</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{\ell+1}_{\mu}=\Delta^{\ell}_{\mu}+\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}M_{\mu\nu}\bm{x}_{\nu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\bm{x}_{\mu}\Delta_{\nu}^{\ell}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">We note that this can be separated into two distinct dynamical systems, one for the first <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> training points</p>
<table id="A2.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{\ell+1}_{\mu}=\Delta^{\ell}_{\mu}-\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}\bm{x}_{\nu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\bm{x}_{\mu}\Delta_{\nu}^{\ell}\ ,\ \mu\in\{1,...,P\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>P</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{\ell+1}_{\mu}=\Delta^{\ell}_{\mu}-\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}\bm{x}_{\nu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\bm{x}_{\mu}\Delta_{\nu}^{\ell}\ ,\ \mu\in\{1,...,P\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">which form a closed dynamical system on the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> labeled training points. From these <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> variables <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Delta_{\mu}^{\ell}\}_{\mu\in[P]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Delta_{\mu}^{\ell}\}_{\mu\in[P]}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can describe how the remaining <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> points evolve</p>
<table id="A2.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta^{\ell+1}_{\mu}=\Delta^{\ell}_{\mu}+\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}\bm{x}_{\nu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\bm{x}_{\mu}\Delta_{\nu}^{\ell}=\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}\bm{x}_{\nu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\bm{x}_{\mu}\Delta_{\nu}^{\ell}\ ,\ \mu\in\{P+1,...,P+K\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>P</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>P</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>ν</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta^{\ell+1}_{\mu}=\Delta^{\ell}_{\mu}+\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}\bm{x}_{\nu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\bm{x}_{\mu}\Delta_{\nu}^{\ell}=\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}\bm{x}_{\nu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\bm{x}_{\mu}\Delta_{\nu}^{\ell}\ ,\ \mu\in\{P+1,...,P+K\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Recurrence</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Instead of defining separate <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> matrices for each layer <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math>, we instead can examine a recurrent model where the weights are tied <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}=\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}=\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math>. We relax this assumption in Appendix <a href="#A7.SS1" title="G.1 Different Parameters for Each Layer ‣ Appendix G Enhancing Realism of the Model ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G.1</span></a> and in many of the settings we analyze recurrence has no impact compared to decoupling layers. Under this constraint, the residual stream of the model has the following dynamics</p>
<table id="A2.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\mu}^{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\mu}^{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta^{\ell}_{\mu}-\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}\bm{x}_{\mu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{x}_{\nu}\ \Delta^{\ell}_{\nu}\ ,\ \mu\in\{1,...,P\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>P</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta^{\ell}_{\mu}-\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}\bm{x}_{\mu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{x}_{\nu}\ \Delta^{\ell}_{\nu}\ ,\ \mu\in\{1,...,P\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\mu}^{\ell+1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\mu}^{\ell+1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Delta_{\mu}^{\ell}+\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}\bm{x}_{\mu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{x}_{\nu}\ \Delta^{\ell}_{\nu}\ ,\ \mu\in\{P+1,...,P+K\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>μ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>P</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>μ</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>ν</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>ν</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Delta_{\mu}^{\ell}+\frac{1}{LP}\sum_{\nu=1}^{P}\bm{x}_{\mu}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{x}_{\nu}\ \Delta^{\ell}_{\nu}\ ,\ \mu\in\{P+1,...,P+K\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Delta}^{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚫</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Delta}^{\ell}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the residual stream variables restricted to the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> unmasked training points in the context. This vector has the residual stream dynamics</p>
<table id="A2.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Delta}^{\ell}=\left(\bm{I}-\frac{1}{LP}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\right)^{\ell}\bm{y}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝚫</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Delta}^{\ell}=\left(\bm{I}-\frac{1}{LP}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\right)^{\ell}\bm{y}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">However, the recursion is different for the test set since these points only receive attention signals from the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> unmasked training tokens. For one of the test points <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, the prediction of the model <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="A2.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\star}=\frac{1}{LP}\bm{x}_{\star}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\bm{h}^{\ell}=\frac{1}{LP}\bm{x}_{\star}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\left(\bm{I}-\frac{1}{LP}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\right)^{\ell}\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\star}=\frac{1}{LP}\bm{x}_{\star}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\bm{h}^{\ell}=\frac{1}{LP}\bm{x}_{\star}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\left(\bm{I}-\frac{1}{LP}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\right)^{\ell}\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Equivalence to Preconditioned In-Context Gradient Descent</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This update rule is equivalent to implementing preconditioned in-context gradient descent steps for a linear regression model <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}\bm{\beta}\cdot\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜷</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}\bm{\beta}\cdot\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. To see this, define an in-context training loss <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{L}}(\bm{\beta},\bm{D})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{L}}(\bm{\beta},\bm{D})</annotation></semantics></math> on the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> labeled training points for context <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{D}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\mathcal{L}}(\bm{D})=\frac{1}{2P}||D^{-1/2}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\beta}-\bm{y}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\mathcal{L}}(\bm{D})=\frac{1}{2P}||D^{-1/2}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\beta}-\bm{y}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Preconditioned gradient descent with learning rate <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D/L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D/L</annotation></semantics></math> and a preconditioner matrix <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> generates the following dynamics on the learned ICL weights <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜷</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E54.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\beta}^{\ell+1}=\bm{\beta}^{\ell}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\ \nabla\mathcal{L}(\bm{\beta}^{\ell},\bm{D})=\bm{\beta}^{\ell}-\frac{\sqrt{D}}{LP}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\left(D^{-1/2}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\beta}^{\ell}-\bm{y}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0.667em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑫</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝚪</mi><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\beta}^{\ell+1}=\bm{\beta}^{\ell}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\ \nabla\mathcal{L}(\bm{\beta}^{\ell},\bm{D})=\bm{\beta}^{\ell}-\frac{\sqrt{D}}{LP}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\left(D^{-1/2}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\beta}^{\ell}-\bm{y}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Defining a variable <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{h}^{\ell}\equiv\bm{y}-D^{-1/2}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\beta}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>≡</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝑿</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝜷</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{h}^{\ell}\equiv\bm{y}-D^{-1/2}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\beta}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math>, we note that this variable satisfies the same recursion as the residual stream variables <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{h}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{h}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> on the training points described above which gives the identical solution <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{h}^{\ell}=\left(\bm{I}-\frac{1}{LP}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\right)^{\ell}\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{h}^{\ell}=\left(\bm{I}-\frac{1}{LP}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\right)^{\ell}\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. The function <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> on a test point <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> takes the form</p>
<table id="A2.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f_{\star}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}\bm{\beta}^{L}\cdot\bm{x}_{\star}=\frac{1}{LP}\bm{x}_{\star}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\bm{h}^{\ell}=\frac{1}{LP}\bm{x}_{\star}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\left(\bm{I}-\frac{1}{LP}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\right)^{\ell}\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒚</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f_{\star}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}\bm{\beta}^{L}\cdot\bm{x}_{\star}=\frac{1}{LP}\bm{x}_{\star}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\bm{h}^{\ell}=\frac{1}{LP}\bm{x}_{\star}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\left(\bm{I}-\frac{1}{LP}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\right)^{\ell}\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We will next express the test loss</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Test Error Formula for Linear Models</h5>

<div id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now desire to compute the expected test loss (averaged over the dataset <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑿</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and noise <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>) for (noisy) linear target function <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y(\bm{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y(\bm{x})</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A2.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle y(\bm{x})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}\bm{\beta}_{\star}\cdot\bm{x}+\sigma\epsilon\ ,\ \left&lt;\bm{x}\bm{x}^{\top}\right&gt;=\bm{\Sigma}\ ,\ \left&lt;\epsilon^{2}\right&gt;=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle y(\bm{x})=\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}\bm{\beta}_{\star}\cdot\bm{x}+\sigma\epsilon\ ,\ \left&lt;\bm{x}\bm{x}^{\top}\right&gt;=\bm{\Sigma}\ ,\ \left&lt;\epsilon^{2}\right&gt;=1</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> is the (population) covariance of the inputs. The expected loss under this assumption is</p>
<table id="A2.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\left(\bm{\beta}^{L}-\bm{\beta}_{\star}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\left(\bm{\beta}^{L}-\bm{\beta}_{\star}\right)\right&gt;_{\bm{X},\bm{\epsilon}}+\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\left(\bm{\beta}^{L}-\bm{\beta}_{\star}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\left(\bm{\beta}^{L}-\bm{\beta}_{\star}\right)\right&gt;_{\bm{X},\bm{\epsilon}}+\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Letting <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the noise on the <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> labeled training points, the target weights have the form</p>
<table id="A2.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\beta}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\beta}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{D}}{LP}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L}\left(\bm{I}-\frac{1}{LP}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\right)^{\ell}\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\beta}_{\star}+\sigma\bm{\epsilon}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\sqrt{D}}{LP}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L}\left(\bm{I}-\frac{1}{LP}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}\right)^{\ell}\left[\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}\bm{X}^{\top}\bm{\beta}_{\star}+\sigma\bm{\epsilon}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell}\bm{\beta}_{\star}+\frac{\sigma\sqrt{D}}{LP}\ \bm{\Gamma}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\bm{\Gamma}\right)^{\ell}\bm{X}\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell}\bm{\beta}_{\star}+\frac{\sigma\sqrt{D}}{LP}\ \bm{\Gamma}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\bm{\Gamma}\right)^{\ell}\bm{X}\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\bm{\beta}_{\star}-\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\bm{\beta}_{\star}+\frac{\sigma\sqrt{D}}{LP}\bm{\Gamma}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\bm{\Gamma}\right)^{\ell}\bm{X}\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\bm{\beta}_{\star}-\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\bm{\beta}_{\star}+\frac{\sigma\sqrt{D}}{LP}\bm{\Gamma}\sum_{\ell=0}^{L-1}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\bm{\Gamma}\right)^{\ell}\bm{X}\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where we defined <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}=\frac{1}{P}\bm{X}\bm{X}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}=\frac{1}{P}\bm{X}\bm{X}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we note that for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\equiv P/D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\equiv P/D</annotation></semantics></math> that the reducible loss <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}-\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}-\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> has the form</p>
<table id="A2.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}-\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}-\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\left(\bm{\beta}_{\star}-\bm{\beta}^{L}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\left(\bm{\beta}_{\star}-\bm{\beta}^{L}\right)\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\left(\bm{\beta}_{\star}-\bm{\beta}^{L}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\left(\bm{\beta}_{\star}-\bm{\beta}^{L}\right)\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\bm{\beta}_{\star}^{\top}\left&lt;\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L\top}\bm{\Sigma}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\right&gt;\bm{\beta}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{D}\bm{\beta}_{\star}^{\top}\left&lt;\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L\top}\bm{\Sigma}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\right&gt;\bm{\beta}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E59.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\alpha L^{2}}\text{Tr}\ \bm{\Gamma}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\sum_{\ell,\ell^{\prime}=0}^{L-1}\left&lt;\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell^{\prime}}\right]^{\top}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mtext>Tr</mtext><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\alpha L^{2}}\text{Tr}\ \bm{\Gamma}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\sum_{\ell,\ell^{\prime}=0}^{L-1}\left&lt;\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell^{\prime}}\right]^{\top}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">In the next sections, we will compute this quantity for various distributions for <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\hat{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\hat{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\beta}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\beta}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Isotropic (<span id="A3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ISO</span>) Setting Theory</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we consider isotropic covariates and tasks so that the data covariance <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and the task vector covariance <math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> are both identity</p>
<table id="A3.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Sigma}=\left&lt;\bm{x}\bm{x}^{\top}\right&gt;=\bm{I}\ ,\ \bm{\Omega}=\left&lt;\bm{\beta}_{\star}\bm{\beta}_{\star}^{\top}\right&gt;=\bm{I}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Sigma}=\left&lt;\bm{x}\bm{x}^{\top}\right&gt;=\bm{I}\ ,\ \bm{\Omega}=\left&lt;\bm{\beta}_{\star}\bm{\beta}_{\star}^{\top}\right&gt;=\bm{I}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the average for target vectors <math id="A3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\beta}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\beta}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is over different contexts. We further operate in the <span id="A3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">high dimensional</span> asymptotic limit where both context length <math id="A3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and input dimension <math id="A3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> diverge with fixed ratio</p>
<table id="A3.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P,D\to\infty\ ,\ P/D=\alpha." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P,D\to\infty\ ,\ P/D=\alpha.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">In this setting, the spectrum of the empirical covariance matrix <math id="A3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}=\frac{1}{P}\bm{X}\bm{X}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}=\frac{1}{P}\bm{X}\bm{X}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> follows the well-known Marchenko-Pastur law, where the eigenvalue density <math id="A3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> depends explicitly on the aspect ratio <math id="A3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Potters &amp; Bouchaud, 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Advani et al., 2020</a>)</cite>. We will first describe an asymptotic limit of SGD for the shallow <math id="A3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=1</annotation></semantics></math> case where the dynamics on the matrix <math id="A3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> are linear. We will then pursue a description of gradient flow dynamics in an arbitrary depth <math id="A3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> model.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Shallow SGD Theory</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we consider the SGD dynamics of the shallow architecture <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=1</annotation></semantics></math>. This excercise will establish at what rate our dynamics will converge to gradient flow and how finite batchsize <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, context length <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and number of masked evaluation points <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> impact the SGD dynamics. In this case, the updates have the form</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Gamma}(t+1)=\bm{\Gamma}(t)+\eta\ \bm{G}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Gamma}(t+1)=\bm{\Gamma}(t)+\eta\ \bm{G}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{G}(t)=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{n}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star,n}\left[(\bm{I}-\bm{\Gamma}\bm{\Sigma}_{n})\bm{\beta}_{n}-\sigma P^{-1}\sqrt{D}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}_{n}\bm{\epsilon}_{n}\right]\left[\bm{\Sigma}_{n}\bm{\beta}_{n}+\sigma P^{-1}\sqrt{D}\bm{X}_{n}\bm{\epsilon}_{n}\right]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>n</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{G}(t)=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{n}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star,n}\left[(\bm{I}-\bm{\Gamma}\bm{\Sigma}_{n})\bm{\beta}_{n}-\sigma P^{-1}\sqrt{D}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}_{n}\bm{\epsilon}_{n}\right]\left[\bm{\Sigma}_{n}\bm{\beta}_{n}+\sigma P^{-1}\sqrt{D}\bm{X}_{n}\bm{\epsilon}_{n}\right]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{n}=\frac{1}{P}\bm{X}_{n}^{\top}\bm{X}_{n}\ ,\ \hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star,n}=\frac{1}{K}\bm{X}_{\star,n}^{\top}\bm{X}_{\star,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>P</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{n}=\frac{1}{P}\bm{X}_{n}^{\top}\bm{X}_{n}\ ,\ \hat{\bm{\Sigma}}_{\star,n}=\frac{1}{K}\bm{X}_{\star,n}^{\top}\bm{X}_{\star,n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{P\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{P\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> is the set of training points and <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}_{\star}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}_{\star}\in\mathbb{R}^{K\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the set of <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> evaluation points and <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\epsilon}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>P</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\epsilon}\in\mathbb{R}^{P}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the label noise on the provided targets <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒚</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. We remind the reader that we will operate in the joint scaling limit</p>
<table id="A3.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P,B,K,D\to\infty\ ,\ P/D=\alpha\ ,\ K/D=\kappa\ ,\ B/D=\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P,B,K,D\to\infty\ ,\ P/D=\alpha\ ,\ K/D=\kappa\ ,\ B/D=\tau</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The population ICL loss has the form</p>
<table id="A3.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)=\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;|\bm{\Gamma}(t)-\bm{I}|^{2}\right&gt;," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)=\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;|\bm{\Gamma}(t)-\bm{I}|^{2}\right&gt;,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where the average is performed over all possible draws of data and tasks. This function admits the recursion</p>
<table id="A3.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t+1)=\mathcal{L}(t)-2\eta\text{tr}[\bm{\Gamma}(t)-\bm{I}]^{\top}\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;+\eta^{2}\text{tr}\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)^{\top}\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t+1)=\mathcal{L}(t)-2\eta\text{tr}[\bm{\Gamma}(t)-\bm{I}]^{\top}\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;+\eta^{2}\text{tr}\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)^{\top}\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">We have the following mean for the gradient</p>
<table id="A3.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;=(\bm{I}-(1+\alpha^{-1}+\sigma^{2}\alpha^{-1})\bm{\Gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;=(\bm{I}-(1+\alpha^{-1}+\sigma^{2}\alpha^{-1})\bm{\Gamma})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Thus if we only updated using mean gradients the model would relax to a fixed point <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}=\left(1+\alpha^{-1}+\sigma^{2}\alpha^{-1}\right)^{-1}\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}=\left(1+\alpha^{-1}+\sigma^{2}\alpha^{-1}\right)^{-1}\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, we will see momentarily that SGD noise in the gradients impact the <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> that SGD converges to</p>
<table id="A3.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{tr}\ \left&lt;\bm{G}(t)^{\top}\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;=\frac{1}{B^{2}}\sum_{nm}\text{tr}\ \left&lt;\bm{u}_{n}\bm{v}_{n}^{\top}\bm{v}_{m}\bm{u}_{m}^{\top}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{tr}\ \left&lt;\bm{G}(t)^{\top}\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;=\frac{1}{B^{2}}\sum_{nm}\text{tr}\ \left&lt;\bm{u}_{n}\bm{v}_{n}^{\top}\bm{v}_{m}\bm{u}_{m}^{\top}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{n}=\bm{\hat{\Sigma}}_{\star,n}\left[(\bm{I}-\bm{\Gamma}\bm{\Sigma}_{n})\bm{\beta}_{n}-\sigma p^{-1}\sqrt{d}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}_{n}\bm{\epsilon}_{n}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo rspace="0em">⋆</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{n}=\bm{\hat{\Sigma}}_{\star,n}\left[(\bm{I}-\bm{\Gamma}\bm{\Sigma}_{n})\bm{\beta}_{n}-\sigma p^{-1}\sqrt{d}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{X}_{n}\bm{\epsilon}_{n}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}_{n}=\bm{\Sigma}_{n}\bm{\beta}_{n}+\sigma p^{-1}\sqrt{d}\bm{X}_{n}\bm{\epsilon}_{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝚺</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}_{n}=\bm{\Sigma}_{n}\bm{\beta}_{n}+\sigma p^{-1}\sqrt{d}\bm{X}_{n}\bm{\epsilon}_{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. Doing the averages</p>
<table id="A3.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\bm{u}_{n}\cdot\bm{u}_{m}\right&gt;=\delta_{mn}\text{tr}\left[\bm{I}-2\bm{\Gamma}+(1+\alpha^{-1})\bm{\Gamma}^{2}+\sigma^{2}\alpha^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}^{2}\right](1+\kappa^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\bm{u}_{n}\cdot\bm{u}_{m}\right&gt;=\delta_{mn}\text{tr}\left[\bm{I}-2\bm{\Gamma}+(1+\alpha^{-1})\bm{\Gamma}^{2}+\sigma^{2}\alpha^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}^{2}\right](1+\kappa^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\delta_{mn}(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))(1+\kappa^{-1})\text{tr}\left[(\bm{\Gamma}-\bm{\Gamma}_{\star})^{2}+\frac{\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})}{(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}}\bm{I}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\delta_{mn}(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))(1+\kappa^{-1})\text{tr}\left[(\bm{\Gamma}-\bm{\Gamma}_{\star})^{2}+\frac{\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})}{(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}}\bm{I}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\bm{v}_{n}\cdot\bm{v}_{m}\right&gt;=\delta_{mn}(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\bm{v}_{n}\cdot\bm{v}_{m}\right&gt;=\delta_{mn}(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.7" class="ltx_p">From the above results, we get the following second moment structure</p>
<table id="A3.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{tr}\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)^{\top}\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑮</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{tr}\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)^{\top}\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{tr}\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;^{\top}\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑮</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{tr}\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;^{\top}\left&lt;\bm{G}(t)\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}\left[(\bm{\Gamma}-\bm{\Gamma}_{\star})^{2}+\frac{\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})}{(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}}\bm{I}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}\left[(\bm{\Gamma}-\bm{\Gamma}_{\star})^{2}+\frac{\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})}{(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}}\bm{I}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Thus we get a recursion</p>
<table id="A3.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{\Gamma}(t+1)=\bm{\Gamma}(t)+\eta(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))\left[\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}-\bm{\Gamma}(t)\right]+\eta\ \bm{\Xi}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚵</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{\Gamma}(t+1)=\bm{\Gamma}(t)+\eta(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))\left[\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}-\bm{\Gamma}(t)\right]+\eta\ \bm{\Xi}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Xi}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚵</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Xi}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> is the noise process with variance given above. We define a quantity <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(t)</annotation></semantics></math> which measures the relaxation of <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A3.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C(t)=\frac{1}{D}\left|\bm{\Gamma}(t)-\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}\right|^{2}\ ,\ \bm{\Gamma}_{\star}=\left[1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})\right]^{-1}\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C(t)=\frac{1}{D}\left|\bm{\Gamma}(t)-\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}\right|^{2}\ ,\ \bm{\Gamma}_{\star}=\left[1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})\right]^{-1}\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">This function exhibits the following linear dynamics</p>
<table id="A3.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C(t+1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C(t+1)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left[1-\eta\left(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})\right)\right]^{2}C(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left[1-\eta\left(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})\right)\right]^{2}C(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\eta^{2}}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}\left[C(t)+\frac{\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})}{(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\eta^{2}}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}\left[C(t)+\frac{\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})}{(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This recursion again takes the form</p>
<table id="A3.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C(t+1)=a(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)C(t)+b(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C(t+1)=a(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)C(t)+b(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle a(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)=\left[1-\eta\left(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})\right)\right]^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle a(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)=\left[1-\eta\left(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})\right)\right]^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle b(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)=\frac{\eta^{2}}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle b(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)=\frac{\eta^{2}}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Now we need to compute the ICL loss</p>
<table id="A3.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{tr}[\bm{\Gamma}(t)-\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}+\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}-\bm{I}]^{2}=C(t)+2\text{tr}(\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}-\bm{\Gamma}(t))(\bm{I}-\bm{\Gamma}_{\star})+\text{tr}(\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}-\bm{I})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{tr}[\bm{\Gamma}(t)-\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}+\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}-\bm{I}]^{2}=C(t)+2\text{tr}(\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}-\bm{\Gamma}(t))(\bm{I}-\bm{\Gamma}_{\star})+\text{tr}(\bm{\Gamma}_{\star}-\bm{I})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C(t)+\frac{2\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})}{(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}}\left[1-\eta(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))\right]^{t}+\frac{(1+\sigma^{2})^{2}}{(\alpha+1+\sigma^{2})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C(t)+\frac{2\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})}{(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}}\left[1-\eta(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))\right]^{t}+\frac{(1+\sigma^{2})^{2}}{(\alpha+1+\sigma^{2})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A3.F7.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01098v1/loss_vary_tau_depth_1_alpha_1.0.svg" id="A3.F7.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:181/139;" width="181" height="139"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Vary Batchsize <math id="A3.F7.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A3.F7.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01098v1/loss_vary_alpha_depth_1_tau_1.0.svg" id="A3.F7.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:176/135;" width="176" height="135"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Vary Context Length <math id="A3.F7.sf2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A3.F7.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01098v1/loss_vary_kappa_depth_1_alpha_1.0.svg" id="A3.F7.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:181/139;" width="181" height="139"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Varying Evaluation Size <math id="A3.F7.sf3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Pretraining SGD loss dynamics in the shallow <math id="A3.F7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=1</annotation></semantics></math> reduced <math id="A3.F7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> model for (a) <math id="A3.F7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\kappa=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\kappa=1</annotation></semantics></math> and varying <math id="A3.F7.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> (b) varying <math id="A3.F7.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.F7.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\kappa=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\kappa=1</annotation></semantics></math> (c) varying <math id="A3.F7.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.F7.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\tau=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\tau=1</annotation></semantics></math>. The loss monotonically improves with all three quantities <math id="A3.F7.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau,\alpha,\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau,\alpha,\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> and is well predicted by the asymptotic theory. </figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Putting this all together, we summarize our findings below.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="160.62" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 160.62" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,160.62) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#0000FF;" fill="#0000FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 154.71 C 0 157.97 2.64 160.62 5.91 160.62 L 544.09 160.62 C 547.36 160.62 550 157.97 550 154.71 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="0.95"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 136.51 L 548.03 136.51 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 145.1)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Result 10: Online SGD Dynamics for Shallow ICL with Isotropic Covariates</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 17.24)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:7.77em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="110.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 107.46)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Consider the reduced <math id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> model with a single layer <math id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=1</annotation></semantics></math> and proportional asymptotics</span></span>
<span id="A3.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A3.E77"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P,K,B,D\to\infty\ ,\ P/D=\alpha\ ,\ K/D=\kappa\ ,\ B/D=\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.500em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.500em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.500em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P,K,B,D\to\infty\ ,\ P/D=\alpha\ ,\ K/D=\kappa\ ,\ B/D=\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Then the ICL test loss <math id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(t)=\frac{1}{d}||\bm{\Gamma}(t)-\bm{I}||^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝑰</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(t)=\frac{1}{d}||\bm{\Gamma}(t)-\bm{I}||^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> after <math id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> SGD iterations is</span></span>
<span id="A3.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="A3.E78"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)=C(t)+\frac{2\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})}{(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}}\left[1-\eta(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))\right]^{t}+\frac{(1+\sigma^{2})^{2}}{(\alpha+1+\sigma^{2})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)=C(t)+\frac{2\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})}{(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}}\left[1-\eta(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))\right]^{t}+\frac{(1+\sigma^{2})^{2}}{(\alpha+1+\sigma^{2})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></span></span></span>
<span id="A3.E79"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C(t)=a(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)^{t}+\frac{1-a(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)^{t}}{1-a(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)}b(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C(t)=a(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)^{t}+\frac{1-a(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)^{t}}{1-a(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)}b(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span>
<span rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)=\left[1-\eta\left(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})\right)\right]^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">]</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)=\left[1-\eta\left(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})\right)\right]^{2}+\frac{\eta^{2}}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})(1+\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)=\frac{\eta^{2}}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">η</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">κ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b(\eta,\alpha,\kappa,\tau)=\frac{\eta^{2}}{\tau}(1+\kappa^{-1})\alpha^{-1}(1+\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> capture the dependence on batchsize through <math id="A3.SS1.p7.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">We verify the validity of these learning curves for shallow pretraining dynamics in Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.1 Shallow SGD Theory ‣ Appendix C Isotropic (ISO) Setting Theory ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">We thus see that deviations from gradient flow in the <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=1</annotation></semantics></math> model come in at a scale of <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta/\tau</annotation></semantics></math>. The purpose of this result is to stress that only <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> total tokens are required (unlike the prior work of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al. (2025)</a></cite> which required <math id="A3.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(D^{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(D^{3})</annotation></semantics></math> tokens) for an ICL learner in this regime <span id="footnote3" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">3</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">3</span>
              
              
              
            The gap is caused by suboptimal scaling of the number of evaluation points <math id="footnote3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> per context (usually <math id="footnote3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=1</annotation></semantics></math> in prior works). Note realistic LLMs get multiple error signals per context (one per token).</span></span></span>. We verify these theoretical learning curves in Figure <a href="#A3.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ C.1 Shallow SGD Theory ‣ Appendix C Isotropic (ISO) Setting Theory ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">We also indicate the following facts about SGD effects</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The number of masked evaluation points per batch <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\equiv K/D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\equiv K/D</annotation></semantics></math> only alters the SGD noise terms (the terms involving <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\tau</annotation></semantics></math>) and its effect vanishes in the gradient flow limit <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta/\tau\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta/\tau\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike offline training, in this online SGD setting the model regularizes the final value of <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)=</annotation></semantics></math> based on label noise <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to reduce overfitting.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">SGD fluctuations can impact the final loss through <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}C(t)=\frac{b(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)}{1-a(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>κ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}C(t)=\frac{b(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)}{1-a(\eta,\alpha,\tau,\kappa)}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS1.p10.2" class="ltx_p">One nice consequence of this result is that the gradient flow limit can be accessed simply by controlling the scale of <math id="A3.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta/\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta/\tau</annotation></semantics></math> in a limit where batch size is <span id="A3.SS1.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">linear</span> in the dimension <math id="A3.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=\tau D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=\tau D</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Gradient Flow in Deep Models</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the previous section, we saw that in the absence of SGD noise, gradient dynamics generated an isotropic <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> matrix. This fact is true for larger depth <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> as well. The gradient flow dynamics generate is <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}(t)=\gamma(t)\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}(t)=\gamma(t)\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. To see this, we note that the gradient has the form</p>
<table id="A3.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex21.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\left&lt;\frac{2}{L}\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell}\right]^{\top}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L-1-\ell}\right]^{\top}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\left&lt;\frac{2}{L}\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell}\right]^{\top}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L-1-\ell}\right]^{\top}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{2\sigma^{2}}{\alpha L^{2}}\bm{\Gamma}\sum_{\ell,\ell^{\prime}}\left&lt;\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell^{\prime}}\right]^{\top}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝚪</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{2\sigma^{2}}{\alpha L^{2}}\bm{\Gamma}\sum_{\ell,\ell^{\prime}}\left&lt;\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell^{\prime}}\right]^{\top}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E80.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{2\sigma^{2}}{\alpha L^{3}}\bm{\Gamma}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\sum_{\ell,\ell^{\prime},k}\left&lt;\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{k}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left(\bm{I}-\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell-1-k}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell^{\prime}}\right]^{\top}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{2\sigma^{2}}{\alpha L^{3}}\bm{\Gamma}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\sum_{\ell,\ell^{\prime},k}\left&lt;\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{k}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left(\bm{I}-\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell-1-k}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell^{\prime}}\right]^{\top}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Now, evaluating this at <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}=\gamma\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}=\gamma\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math> we find</p>
<table id="A3.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}\mathcal{L}|_{\bm{\Gamma}=\gamma\bm{I}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}\mathcal{L}|_{\bm{\Gamma}=\gamma\bm{I}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-2\left&lt;\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{2L-1}\right&gt;+\frac{2\sigma^{2}\gamma}{\alpha L^{2}}\left&lt;\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\sum_{\ell\ell^{\prime}}(1-L^{-1}\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}})^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-2\left&lt;\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{2L-1}\right&gt;+\frac{2\sigma^{2}\gamma}{\alpha L^{2}}\left&lt;\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\sum_{\ell\ell^{\prime}}(1-L^{-1}\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}})^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E81.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{2\sigma^{2}\gamma^{2}}{\alpha L^{2}}\sum_{\ell,\ell^{\prime}}\left&lt;\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}-1}\right&gt;\propto\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>γ</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{2\sigma^{2}\gamma^{2}}{\alpha L^{2}}\sum_{\ell,\ell^{\prime}}\left&lt;\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{\ell+\ell^{\prime}-1}\right&gt;\propto\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where we recognize through rotational invariance, that the above averages are proportional to the identity. Thus if <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> is currently in an isotropic configuration, it will remain in one throughout gradient flow. Further, we can compute the scalar <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)=\text{tr}\bm{\Gamma}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)=\text{tr}\bm{\Gamma}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> under gradient flow <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\partial_{t}\bm{\Gamma}(t)=-\frac{1}{2}\partial_{\bm{\Gamma}}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\Gamma})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mi>𝚪</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial_{t}\bm{\Gamma}(t)=-\frac{1}{2}\partial_{\bm{\Gamma}}\mathcal{L}(\bm{\Gamma})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A3.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\gamma(t)=-\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma}\text{tr}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{2L}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\alpha}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}^{-1}\left[\bm{I}-\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\right]^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\gamma(t)=-\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma}\text{tr}\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{2L}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\alpha}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}^{-1}\left[\bm{I}-\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\right]^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Now, we note that this expression can be rewritten in terms of the Marchenko-Pastur eigenvalue density <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\lambda)=\frac{1}{D}\sum_{k=1}^{D}\left&lt;\delta(\lambda-\lambda_{k})\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\lambda)=\frac{1}{D}\sum_{k=1}^{D}\left&lt;\delta(\lambda-\lambda_{k})\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> as</p>
<table id="A3.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E83.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\gamma(t)=-\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma}\int d\lambda\rho(\lambda)\left[\left(1-L^{-1}\gamma\lambda\right)^{2L}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\alpha\lambda}\left[1-\left(1-L^{-1}\gamma\lambda\right)^{L}\right]^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\gamma(t)=-\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma}\int d\lambda\rho(\lambda)\left[\left(1-L^{-1}\gamma\lambda\right)^{2L}+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{\alpha\lambda}\left[1-\left(1-L^{-1}\gamma\lambda\right)^{L}\right]^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">which shows that we can view the dynamics as a gradient flow on a one dimensional loss landscape.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Fixed and Structured Covariance (<span id="A4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">FS</span>) Setting</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section we discuss the case where the data covariance is structured but potentially structured. We consider the noise free setting and <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P/D\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P/D\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity where the loss has the form</p>
<table id="A4.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\left&lt;\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\right]^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\left&lt;\left[\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\right]^{\top}\bm{\Sigma}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{\Gamma}{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In this case, gradient flow will generate dynamics that cause <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> to pick up anisotropy from the structure of <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>. We analyze the case where <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝛀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> are simultaneously diagonalizable with eigenvalues <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, <math id="A4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> will share the same eigenbasis. Let the eigenvalues be <math id="A4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A4.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\gamma_{k}(t)=2\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}^{2}\left(1-L^{-1}\lambda_{k}\gamma_{k}(t)\right)^{2L-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\gamma_{k}(t)=2\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}^{2}\left(1-L^{-1}\lambda_{k}\gamma_{k}(t)\right)^{2L-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(85)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The fixed point of the above dynamics is <math id="A4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{k}=L\lambda_{k}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{k}=L\lambda_{k}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. In the large depth limit <math id="A4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we can solve the dynamics exactly</p>
<table id="A4.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\gamma_{k}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\gamma_{k}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}^{2}e^{-2\lambda_{k}\gamma_{k}(t)}\implies e^{2\lambda_{k}\gamma_{k}}d\gamma_{k}=\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}^{2}dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}^{2}e^{-2\lambda_{k}\gamma_{k}(t)}\implies e^{2\lambda_{k}\gamma_{k}}d\gamma_{k}=\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}^{2}dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\implies 2\lambda_{k}\gamma_{k}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\implies 2\lambda_{k}\gamma_{k}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E86.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ln(1+4\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}^{3}t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ln</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ln(1+4\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}^{3}t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(86)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Plugging this solution into the loss function we find</p>
<table id="A4.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)=\frac{1}{D}\sum_{k}\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}e^{-2\gamma_{k}\lambda_{k}}=\frac{1}{D}\sum_{k}\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}[1+\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}^{3}t]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)=\frac{1}{D}\sum_{k}\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}e^{-2\gamma_{k}\lambda_{k}}=\frac{1}{D}\sum_{k}\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}[1+\omega_{k}\lambda_{k}^{3}t]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(87)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Under powerlaw (source/capacity) assumptions on the structure of the data</p>
<table id="A4.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda_{k}\sim k^{-\nu}\ ,\ \omega_{k}\lambda_{k}\sim k^{-\nu\beta-1}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda_{k}\sim k^{-\nu}\ ,\ \omega_{k}\lambda_{k}\sim k^{-\nu\beta-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(88)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">the loss scales in a powerlaw as</p>
<table id="A4.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)=\sum_{k}k^{-\nu\beta-1}[1+k^{-2\nu-\nu\beta}t]^{-1}\sim t^{-\frac{\beta}{\nu+\nu\beta+1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)=\sum_{k}k^{-\nu\beta-1}[1+k^{-2\nu-\nu\beta}t]^{-1}\sim t^{-\frac{\beta}{\nu+\nu\beta+1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(89)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p2.3" class="ltx_p">This powerlaw provides a decent approximation to large but finite depth models <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> as we show in Figure <a href="#S3.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 3.2 Fixed Structured Covariance (FS) → Preconditioned Gradient Descent ‣ 3 Learning Curves in Reduced Linear Attention Model ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Randomly Rotated and Structured Covariance (<span id="A5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RRS</span>) Setting</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Exploiting Symmetry in the Gradient Updates</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Utilizing the definition of the RRS setting, we can massage the placement of the orthogonal matrices so that the loss function can be expressed as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\left&lt;|\bm{\Lambda}^{1/2}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{O}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{O}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\bm{\beta}_{\star}|^{2}\right&gt;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑶</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\left&lt;|\bm{\Lambda}^{1/2}\left(\bm{I}-L^{-1}\bm{O}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{O}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\bm{\beta}_{\star}|^{2}\right&gt;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(90)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">From this expression, it is immediately clear that this function is rotationally invariant with respect to <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> since the transformation <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}\to\bm{V}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{V}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}\to\bm{V}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{V}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> for orthogonal <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{V}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{V}</annotation></semantics></math> leaves the Haar average unchanged. The form of the loss gradients also reveals a symmetry</p>
<table id="A5.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E91.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}\mathcal{L}=-2L^{-1}\sum_{\ell}\left&lt;\bm{O}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\bm{M}^{\ell}\bm{\beta}_{\star}\bm{\beta}_{\star}^{\top}\left(\bm{M}^{L}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\bm{M}^{L-1-\ell}\right)^{\top}\bm{O}^{\top}\right&gt;\ ,\ \bm{M}=\bm{I}-\bm{O}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{O}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝑶</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝚲</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>𝑶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.500em">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝑶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi>𝑶</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}\mathcal{L}=-2L^{-1}\sum_{\ell}\left&lt;\bm{O}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\bm{M}^{\ell}\bm{\beta}_{\star}\bm{\beta}_{\star}^{\top}\left(\bm{M}^{L}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\bm{M}^{L-1-\ell}\right)^{\top}\bm{O}^{\top}\right&gt;\ ,\ \bm{M}=\bm{I}-\bm{O}^{\top}\bm{\Gamma}\bm{O}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(91)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Note that starting from zero initialization, we have <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}=0</annotation></semantics></math> which implies isotropic gradients <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}\mathcal{L}|_{\bm{\Gamma}=0}\propto\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∝</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}\mathcal{L}|_{\bm{\Gamma}=0}\propto\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math>. To see this note that <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left&lt;\bm{O}\bm{C}\bm{O}^{\top}\right&gt;\propto\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝑶</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>∝</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left&lt;\bm{O}\bm{C}\bm{O}^{\top}\right&gt;\propto\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math> for any matrix <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{C}</annotation></semantics></math> that is independent of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{O}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, suppose that we evaluated the loss gradient at any isotropic <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}=\gamma\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝚪</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}=\gamma\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}=\bm{I}-\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}=\bm{I}-\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the gradients remain isotropic</p>
<table id="A5.EGx85" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E92.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-2L^{-1}\sum_{\ell}\left&lt;\bm{O}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\bm{M}^{\ell}\bm{\beta}_{\star}\bm{\beta}_{\star}^{\top}\left(\bm{M}^{L}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\bm{M}^{L-1-\ell}\right)^{\top}\bm{O}^{\top}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mi>𝑶</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝚲</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mi>𝑶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-2L^{-1}\sum_{\ell}\left&lt;\bm{O}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\bm{M}^{\ell}\bm{\beta}_{\star}\bm{\beta}_{\star}^{\top}\left(\bm{M}^{L}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\bm{M}^{L-1-\ell}\right)^{\top}\bm{O}^{\top}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(92)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E93.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-2L^{-1}\sum_{\ell}\text{tr}\left&lt;\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\bm{M}^{\ell}\bm{\beta}_{\star}\bm{\beta}_{\star}^{\top}\left(\bm{M}^{L}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\bm{M}^{L-1-\ell}\right)^{\top}\right&gt;\times\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><mtext>tr</mtext><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝚲</mi><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>𝑴</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">⟩</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-2L^{-1}\sum_{\ell}\text{tr}\left&lt;\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\bm{M}^{\ell}\bm{\beta}_{\star}\bm{\beta}_{\star}^{\top}\left(\bm{M}^{L}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\bm{M}^{L-1-\ell}\right)^{\top}\right&gt;\times\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(93)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">where we explicitly performed the average over the only remaining factors of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{O}</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}=\bm{I}-\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}=\bm{I}-\gamma\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{O}</annotation></semantics></math>. Further, we can express the dynamics of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> as a gradient flow on the reduced one-dimensional loss landscape</p>
<table id="A5.EGx86" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\gamma)=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\gamma)=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(94)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Scaling Law Theory</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we consider the scaling law theory with a finite projection matrix <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}</annotation></semantics></math>, following <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bordelon et al. (2024a)</a></cite>. In this case, our <span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RRS</span> setting requires utilizing the free product result in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Two Point Deterministic Equivalent for General Free Product From Dynamical Mean Field Theory ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Dynamics at Infinite <math id="A6.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,L,P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,L,P</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The gradient flow in the limit of <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,L,P\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,L,P\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> has the form</p>
<table id="A6.EGx87" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E95.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\gamma(t)=-\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma}\sum_{k}\lambda_{k}\omega_{k}e^{-2\gamma(t)\lambda_{k}}\approx-\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma}\gamma(t)^{-\beta}=\beta\gamma(t)^{-\beta-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>γ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0em">≈</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>γ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>γ</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{d}{dt}\gamma(t)=-\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma}\sum_{k}\lambda_{k}\omega_{k}e^{-2\gamma(t)\lambda_{k}}\approx-\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma}\gamma(t)^{-\beta}=\beta\gamma(t)^{-\beta-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(95)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">This is a separable ODE with solution (under the assumption that <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math>) up to constants</p>
<table id="A6.EGx88" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma(t)\sim t^{\frac{1}{\beta+2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma(t)\sim t^{\frac{1}{\beta+2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(96)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">This implies a powerlaw loss scaling with exponent set by the rate of growth of <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A6.EGx89" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)\sim\gamma(t)^{-\beta}\sim t^{-\frac{\beta}{2+\beta}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>β</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(t)\sim\gamma(t)^{-\beta}\sim t^{-\frac{\beta}{2+\beta}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(97)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We expect these dynamics to hold in the limit of <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,L,P\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,L,P\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. At finite <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,L,P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,L,P</annotation></semantics></math> the model will saturate at some finite maximal value of <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Depth Scaling Law at Infinite Time, Width, and Context Length</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now explore the scaling law in depth <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, we can consider taking all other resources to infinity <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t,N,P\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t,N,P\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. The value of <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> will stabilize, resulting in a final loss</p>
<table id="A6.EGx90" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\gamma)=\sum_{k}\lambda_{k}\omega_{k}\left(1-\gamma L^{-1}\lambda_{k}\right)^{2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\gamma)=\sum_{k}\lambda_{k}\omega_{k}\left(1-\gamma L^{-1}\lambda_{k}\right)^{2L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(98)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">While <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> diverges as <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t^{\frac{1}{2+\beta}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t^{\frac{1}{2+\beta}}</annotation></semantics></math> in the infinite depth limit, we see that at large but finite depth, there is a maximal <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> which enables stability along the top eigendirection. Specifically we need <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma&lt;\frac{2L}{\lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma&lt;\frac{2L}{\lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and approximate the optimal value s</p>
<table id="A6.EGx91" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\gamma_{\star}\approx L/\lambda_{1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\gamma_{\star}\approx L/\lambda_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(99)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the top (maximal eigenvalue). At <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, the error takes the form</p>
<table id="A6.EGx92" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}\approx\sum_{k}\lambda_{k}(\beta^{\star}_{k})^{2}\left(1-\lambda_{k}/\lambda_{1}\right)^{L}\approx\int dkk^{-\nu\beta-1}\exp(-Lk^{-\nu})\approx L^{-\beta}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}\approx\sum_{k}\lambda_{k}(\beta^{\star}_{k})^{2}\left(1-\lambda_{k}/\lambda_{1}\right)^{L}\approx\int dkk^{-\nu\beta-1}\exp(-Lk^{-\nu})\approx L^{-\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(100)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which matches the scaling of <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> steps of gradient descent on a problem with source exponent <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bordelon &amp; Pehlevan (2021)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Mapping the Loss Function to a Two Point Deterministic Equivalent</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We utilize dynamical mean field theory (DMFT) result of Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Two Point Deterministic Equivalent for General Free Product From Dynamical Mean Field Theory ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a> to compute the effective loss as a function of <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N,L</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. We start with a representation of the relevant polynomial in <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{M}</annotation></semantics></math> with the Cauchy integral formula</p>
<table id="A6.EGx93" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E101"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E101.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\bm{M}\right)^{L}=\int_{\mathcal{C}}\frac{d\omega}{2\pi}\left[i\omega+\bm{M}\right]^{-1}\left(1+\gamma L^{-1}i\omega\right)^{L}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\bm{M}\right)^{L}=\int_{\mathcal{C}}\frac{d\omega}{2\pi}\left[i\omega+\bm{M}\right]^{-1}\left(1+\gamma L^{-1}i\omega\right)^{L},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(101)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the contour <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> encloses the positive imaginary axis in complex plane <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bender &amp; Orszag, 2013</a>)</cite>. Next, we define <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}(\gamma)=\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\bm{M}\right)^{L}\bm{\beta}_{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}(\gamma)=\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\bm{M}\right)^{L}\bm{\beta}_{\star}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A6.EGx94" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\bm{v}(\gamma)^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\bm{v}(\gamma)\right&gt;=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\left[\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\bm{M}\right)^{L}\right]^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\bm{M}\right)^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\bm{v}(\gamma)^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\bm{v}(\gamma)\right&gt;=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\left[\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\bm{M}\right)^{L}\right]^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\bm{I}-\gamma L^{-1}\bm{M}\right)^{L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(102)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">The loss can thus be expressed as a double integral involving the resolvents</p>
<table id="A6.EGx95" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\int_{\mathcal{C}\times\mathcal{C}}\frac{d\omega d\omega^{\prime}}{(2\pi)^{2}}(1+\gamma L^{-1}i\omega)^{L}(1+\gamma L^{-1}i\omega^{\prime})^{L}\ \ \text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\left[\left[i\omega+\bm{M}\right]^{-1}\right]^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left[i\omega^{\prime}+\bm{M}\right]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\int_{\mathcal{C}\times\mathcal{C}}\frac{d\omega d\omega^{\prime}}{(2\pi)^{2}}(1+\gamma L^{-1}i\omega)^{L}(1+\gamma L^{-1}i\omega^{\prime})^{L}\ \ \text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\left[\left[i\omega+\bm{M}\right]^{-1}\right]^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left[i\omega^{\prime}+\bm{M}\right]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(103)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The main result needed is the following deterministic equivalent from Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Two Point Deterministic Equivalent for General Free Product From Dynamical Mean Field Theory ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
<table id="A6.EGx96" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\ \left[\left[i\omega+\bm{M}\right]^{-1}\right]^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left[i\omega^{\prime}+\bm{M}\right]^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\ \left[\left[i\omega+\bm{M}\right]^{-1}\right]^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left[i\omega^{\prime}+\bm{M}\right]^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E104"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\simeq\text{tr}\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\left[\bm{\Omega}-\bm{I}\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\right]\left(i\omega^{\prime}+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\bm{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≃</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝛀</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ω</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\simeq\text{tr}\left(i\omega+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\left[\bm{\Omega}-\bm{I}\Psi_{\chi\chi}(\omega,\omega^{\prime})\right]\left(i\omega^{\prime}+\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega^{\prime})\bm{A}\right)^{-1}\bm{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(104)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.5" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)=i\omega/i\omega_{(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{v\chi}(\omega)=i\omega/i\omega_{(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be determined from the equation</p>
<table id="A6.EGx97" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle i\omega_{(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}}(\tau)i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}(\tau)=\frac{1-\tau}{\tau}(i\omega)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle i\omega_{(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}}(\tau)i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}(\tau)=\frac{1-\tau}{\tau}(i\omega)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(105)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Once <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> is identified as a function of <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math>, we can compute <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{v\chi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{v\chi}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{\chi\chi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mi>χ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>χ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{\chi\chi}</annotation></semantics></math> from the formulae in <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Two Point Deterministic Equivalent for General Free Product From Dynamical Mean Field Theory ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.4 </span>Orthogonal projection and A is Structured Wishart</h3>

<div id="A6.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we describe what these relations imply for a product matrix that arises in our <span id="A6.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RRS</span> setting, which is a free product of the width projection matrix <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> has rank at most <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and the empirical covariance for data in the context <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}=\frac{1}{P}\bm{X}\bm{X}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>P</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}=\frac{1}{P}\bm{X}\bm{X}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.EGx98" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{M}=\bm{O}\ \left(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A}\right)^{2}\ \bm{O}^{\top}\ \hat{\bm{\Sigma}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑶</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{M}=\bm{O}\ \left(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A}\right)^{2}\ \bm{O}^{\top}\ \hat{\bm{\Sigma}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(106)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑶</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{O}</annotation></semantics></math> is a random orthogonal matrix sampled from the Haar measure. The data <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{P\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}\in\mathbb{R}^{P\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> are comprised of random iid vectors with covariance <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, which we take to be diagonal without loss of generality. Further, we let <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A}</annotation></semantics></math> be a rank <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> projection matrix</p>
<table id="A6.EGx99" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E107"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A}=\sum_{k=1}^{N}\bm{e}_{k}\bm{e}_{k}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A}=\sum_{k=1}^{N}\bm{e}_{k}\bm{e}_{k}^{\top}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(107)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{e}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{e}_{k}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> are Cartesian (one-hot) unit vectors. To utilize the result in Appendix <a href="#A1" title="Appendix A Two Point Deterministic Equivalent for General Free Product From Dynamical Mean Field Theory ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A</span></a>, we first need to compute the necessary resolvents for these two matrices. Let <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{N}\equiv N/D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{N}\equiv N/D</annotation></semantics></math> be the ratio between width <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and input dimension <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{P}=\frac{P}{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>P</mi><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{P}=\frac{P}{D}</annotation></semantics></math> represent the ratio of context length to input dimension, then</p>
<table id="A6.EGx100" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E108"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau=\text{tr}(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}\left(i\omega_{(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}}+(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}\right)^{-1}=\frac{\alpha_{N}}{i\omega_{(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}}+1}\implies i\omega_{(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}}=-1+\frac{\alpha_{N}}{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau=\text{tr}(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}\left(i\omega_{(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}}+(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}\right)^{-1}=\frac{\alpha_{N}}{i\omega_{(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}}+1}\implies i\omega_{(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A})^{2}}=-1+\frac{\alpha_{N}}{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(108)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">The other matrix can be easily worked out for a structured Wishart with <math id="A6.SS4.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P/D=\alpha_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P/D=\alpha_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> following the techniques of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bordelon et al. (2024a)</a></cite> which reveals that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx101" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau=\text{tr}\ \hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}+\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{-1}=\text{tr}\bm{\Lambda}\left(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}(1-\alpha_{P}^{-1}\tau)^{-1}+\bm{\Lambda}\right)^{-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau=\text{tr}\ \hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\left(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}+\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}\right)^{-1}=\text{tr}\bm{\Lambda}\left(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}(1-\alpha_{P}^{-1}\tau)^{-1}+\bm{\Lambda}\right)^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(109)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using our result for products we find</p>
<table id="A6.EGx102" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(-1+\frac{\alpha_{N}}{\tau}\right)\left(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}(\tau)\right)=\left(-1+\frac{1}{\tau}\right)i\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(-1+\frac{\alpha_{N}}{\tau}\right)\left(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}(\tau)\right)=\left(-1+\frac{1}{\tau}\right)i\omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau=\text{tr}\bm{\Lambda}\left(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}(1-\alpha_{P}^{-1}\tau)^{-1}+\bm{\Lambda}\right)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau=\text{tr}\bm{\Lambda}\left(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}(1-\alpha_{P}^{-1}\tau)^{-1}+\bm{\Lambda}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.E110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{tr}\bm{\Lambda}\left(i\omega\ (-1+\tau^{-1})(-1+\alpha_{N}/\tau)^{-1}(1-\tau/\alpha_{P})^{-1}+\bm{\Lambda}\right)^{-1}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{tr}\bm{\Lambda}\left(i\omega\ (-1+\tau^{-1})(-1+\alpha_{N}/\tau)^{-1}(1-\tau/\alpha_{P})^{-1}+\bm{\Lambda}\right)^{-1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(110)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Width Bottleneck</h5>

<div id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Now we obtain the scaling of the loss with width <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> in the regime where <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t,P,L,D\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t,P,L,D\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>. To do, we examining the structure of the equations at <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{P}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{P}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\omega\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\omega\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, which correspond to taking gradient flow time <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> (which is the correct solution for noise free problems at infinite depth). In this limit <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\alpha_{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\alpha_{N}</annotation></semantics></math> so we have that</p>
<table id="A6.EGx103" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tau=\frac{N}{D}=\text{tr}\bm{\Lambda}\left(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}+\bm{\Lambda}\right)^{-1}=\frac{1}{D}\sum_{k=1}^{D}\frac{\lambda_{k}}{i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}+\lambda_{k}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>D</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tau=\frac{N}{D}=\text{tr}\bm{\Lambda}\left(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}+\bm{\Lambda}\right)^{-1}=\frac{1}{D}\sum_{k=1}^{D}\frac{\lambda_{k}}{i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}+\lambda_{k}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(111)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For powerlaw features <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{k}\sim k^{-\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{k}\sim k^{-\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> we find an approximate solution for <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A6.EGx104" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lambda_{k}\sim k^{-\nu}\implies i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}\approx N^{-\nu}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lambda_{k}\sim k^{-\nu}\implies i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}\approx N^{-\nu}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(112)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus the loss at width <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and context length <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> can be approximated as</p>
<table id="A6.EGx105" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lim_{t,L,P\to\infty}\mathcal{L}(t,N,P,L)=\sum_{k}\frac{(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}})^{2}\lambda_{k}(\beta^{\star}_{k})^{2}}{(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}+\lambda_{k})^{2}}\sim\sum_{k}\frac{k^{-\nu\beta-1}}{(1+k^{-\nu}N^{\nu})}\approx N^{-\nu\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lim_{t,L,P\to\infty}\mathcal{L}(t,N,P,L)=\sum_{k}\frac{(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}})^{2}\lambda_{k}(\beta^{\star}_{k})^{2}}{(i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}+\lambda_{k})^{2}}\sim\sum_{k}\frac{k^{-\nu\beta-1}}{(1+k^{-\nu}N^{\nu})}\approx N^{-\nu\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(113)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Context Bottleneck</h5>

<div id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Following the same logic, we can investigate the regime where performance is limited by context <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>. To access an approximation for this regime, we take <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{N}\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{N}\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\omega\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\omega\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, we have <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\omega=i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ω</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\omega=i\omega_{\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha_{P}/\tau\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha_{P}/\tau\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\omega\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\omega\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we introduce the leading order behavior for small <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\omega</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A6.EGx106" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 1-\frac{\alpha_{P}}{\tau}\sim r^{-1}i\omega\ ,\ i\omega\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 1-\frac{\alpha_{P}}{\tau}\sim r^{-1}i\omega\ ,\ i\omega\to 0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(114)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> is a (currently) unknown value. Plugging this into the self consistency equation, we identify the value of <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A6.EGx107" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E115.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle P=\sum_{k}\frac{\lambda_{k}}{r+\lambda_{k}}\approx r^{-\frac{1}{\nu}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>ν</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle P=\sum_{k}\frac{\lambda_{k}}{r+\lambda_{k}}\approx r^{-\frac{1}{\nu}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(115)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">which gives the scaling <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\approx P^{-\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≈</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\approx P^{-\nu}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can now use the final value of the resolvent <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(i\omega+\bm{\Lambda}\right)^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(i\omega+\bm{\Lambda}\right)^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A6.EGx108" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E116"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\sum_{k}\frac{r^{2}\lambda_{k}(\beta^{\star}_{k})^{2}}{(r+\lambda_{k})^{2}}\approx\sum_{k}\frac{k^{-\nu\beta-1}}{(1+k^{-\nu}P^{\nu})^{2}}\sim P^{-\nu\beta}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>k</mi></munder></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mi>ν</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=\sum_{k}\frac{r^{2}\lambda_{k}(\beta^{\star}_{k})^{2}}{(r+\lambda_{k})^{2}}\approx\sum_{k}\frac{k^{-\nu\beta-1}}{(1+k^{-\nu}P^{\nu})^{2}}\sim P^{-\nu\beta}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(116)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Rank Deficiency/Null Space Interpretation</h5>

<div id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These last two scaling laws express the simple fact that rank <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> or rank <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> matrices only allow the top <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A6.SS4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> eigendirections to be learned <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bordelon et al., 2024a</a>)</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Enhancing Realism of the Model</h2>

<section id="A7.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.1 </span>Different Parameters for Each Layer</h3>

<div id="A7.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we analyze the case where the model is allowed <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> distinct attention layers along the residual stream <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}\}_{\ell=1}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math> instead of a single attention layer matrix <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> which is applied <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> times recurrently. We focus our attention on the RRS setting at large width and large context length where the model still exhibits nontrivial depth and pretraining time scaling laws. We first consider the noise free setting <math id="A7.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}=0</annotation></semantics></math> before considering the role of target noise.</p>
</div>
<section id="A7.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.1.1 </span>Noise Free Loss Function at Large Width and Context Length</h4>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, we note that by the rotational invariance, each of the matrices is isotropic <math id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}=\gamma^{\ell}\bm{I}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝚪</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}^{\ell}=\gamma^{\ell}\bm{I}</annotation></semantics></math> so that</p>
<table id="A7.EGx109" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\{\gamma^{\ell}\})=\left&lt;\left|\bm{\Lambda}^{1/2}\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\left[\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma^{\ell}\bm{M}\right]\bar{\bm{\beta}}\right|^{2}\right&gt;\ ,\ \bm{M}=\bm{O}\left(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A}\right)^{2}\bm{O}^{\top}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.500em">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑴</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑶</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑶</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\{\gamma^{\ell}\})=\left&lt;\left|\bm{\Lambda}^{1/2}\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\left[\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma^{\ell}\bm{M}\right]\bar{\bm{\beta}}\right|^{2}\right&gt;\ ,\ \bm{M}=\bm{O}\left(\bm{A}^{\top}\bm{A}\right)^{2}\bm{O}^{\top}\hat{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(117)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We note that, due to commutativity of the matrix products <math id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\left[\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma^{\ell}\bm{M}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\left[\bm{I}-L^{-1}\gamma^{\ell}\bm{M}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>, which means that this loss function is permutation symmetric in the <math id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\gamma^{\ell}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\gamma^{\ell}\}</annotation></semantics></math> variables. We therefore expect permutation symmetric dynamics and a solution where <math id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\ell}=\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\ell}=\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, analyzing the gradient flow from <math id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\ell}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\ell}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell</annotation></semantics></math> leads to a balanced solution where all of these are equal since</p>
<table id="A7.EGx110" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma^{\ell}}\mathcal{L}(\{\gamma^{\ell}\})|_{\gamma^{k}=\gamma}=\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma^{\ell^{\prime}}}\mathcal{L}(\{\gamma^{\ell}\})|_{\gamma^{k}=\gamma}\ ,\ \forall\ell,\ell^{\prime}\in\{1,...,L\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma^{\ell}}\mathcal{L}(\{\gamma^{\ell}\})|_{\gamma^{k}=\gamma}=\frac{\partial}{\partial\gamma^{\ell^{\prime}}}\mathcal{L}(\{\gamma^{\ell}\})|_{\gamma^{k}=\gamma}\ ,\ \forall\ell,\ell^{\prime}\in\{1,...,L\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(118)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Thus gradient flow will maintain a balance in these parameters. Further, this flow will exactly match the dynamics of the recurrent model if the learning rate is upscaled by <math id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>. We plot these dynamics and show balancing of the <math id="A7.SS1.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{\ell}(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{\ell}(t)</annotation></semantics></math> variables in Figure <a href="#A7.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ G.1.1 Noise Free Loss Function at Large Width and Context Length ‣ G.1 Different Parameters for Each Layer ‣ Appendix G Enhancing Realism of the Model ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A7.F8" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01098v1/decoupled_layers_powerlaw_dynamics.svg" id="A7.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:209/156;" width="209" height="156"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01098v1/gamma_ells_balanced_powerlaw.svg" id="A7.F8.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:247/149;" width="247" height="149"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span>Dynamics for layer-decoupled reduced <math id="A7.F8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> model. (a) The loss dynamics under powerlaw RRS covariates exhibit the same powerlaws. (b) The different scale factors remain balanced throughout gradient flow <math id="A7.F8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{k}(t)=\gamma(t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{k}(t)=\gamma(t)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A7.F8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in\{1,...,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in\{1,...,L\}</annotation></semantics></math> due to permutation symmetry. </figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">G.1.2 </span>Noisy Target Function</h4>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The predictor in the case of a noisy target function with decoupled layers can be expressed in terms of the evolution of the weight discrepancy <math id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}^{\ell}\equiv\bar{\bm{\beta}}-\hat{\bm{\beta}}^{\ell}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>≡</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}^{\ell}\equiv\bar{\bm{\beta}}-\hat{\bm{\beta}}^{\ell}</annotation></semantics></math> which has the recursion</p>
<table id="A7.EGx111" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{v}^{\ell}=\bm{v}^{\ell-1}-\gamma^{\ell}L^{-1}\bm{M}\bm{v}^{\ell-1}-\frac{\sigma\sqrt{D}}{P}\gamma^{\ell}L^{-1}\bm{X}\bm{\epsilon}\ ,\ \ell\in\{1,...,L\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mrow><mi>P</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{v}^{\ell}=\bm{v}^{\ell-1}-\gamma^{\ell}L^{-1}\bm{M}\bm{v}^{\ell-1}-\frac{\sigma\sqrt{D}}{P}\gamma^{\ell}L^{-1}\bm{X}\bm{\epsilon}\ ,\ \ell\in\{1,...,L\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(119)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Defining the matrices <math id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}^{\ell}=\left[\bm{I}-\gamma^{\ell}L^{-1}\bm{M}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}^{\ell}=\left[\bm{I}-\gamma^{\ell}L^{-1}\bm{M}\right]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{b}=\frac{\sigma\sqrt{D}}{LP}\bm{X}\bm{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϵ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{b}=\frac{\sigma\sqrt{D}}{LP}\bm{X}\bm{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}^{\ell}=\bm{A}^{\ell}\bm{v}^{\ell-1}+\gamma^{\ell}\bm{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}^{\ell}=\bm{A}^{\ell}\bm{v}^{\ell-1}+\gamma^{\ell}\bm{b}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A7.EGx112" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{v}^{L}=\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\bm{A}^{\ell}\bar{\bm{\beta}}+\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\gamma^{\ell}\left(\prod_{k=\ell+1}^{L}\bm{A}^{k}\right)\bm{b}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{v}^{L}=\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\bm{A}^{\ell}\bar{\bm{\beta}}+\sum_{\ell=1}^{L}\gamma^{\ell}\left(\prod_{k=\ell+1}^{L}\bm{A}^{k}\right)\bm{b}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(120)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Since the loss function takes the form <math id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\bm{v}^{L}\cdot\bm{\Lambda}\bm{v}^{L}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>L</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\bm{v}^{L}\cdot\bm{\Lambda}\bm{v}^{L}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> we have</p>
<table id="A7.EGx113" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\bar{\bm{\beta}}^{\top}\left(\prod_{\ell}\bm{A}^{\ell}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\prod_{\ell}\bm{A}^{\ell}\right)\bar{\bm{\beta}}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\bar{\bm{\beta}}^{\top}\left(\prod_{\ell}\bm{A}^{\ell}\right)^{\top}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\prod_{\ell}\bm{A}^{\ell}\right)\bar{\bm{\beta}}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A7.E121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E121.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{D}\sum_{\ell\ell^{\prime}}\gamma^{\ell}\gamma^{\ell^{\prime}}\left&lt;\bm{b}^{\top}\left(\prod_{k=\ell+1}^{L}\bm{A}^{k}\right)\bm{\Lambda}\left(\prod_{k=\ell^{\prime}+1}^{L}\bm{A}^{k}\right)\bm{b}\right&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><msup><mi>γ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{D}\sum_{\ell\ell^{\prime}}\gamma^{\ell}\gamma^{\ell^{\prime}}\left&lt;\bm{b}^{\top}\left(\prod_{k=\ell+1}^{L}\bm{A}^{k}\right)\bm{\Lambda}\left(\prod_{k=\ell^{\prime}+1}^{L}\bm{A}^{k}\right)\bm{b}\right&gt;</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(121)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Using the fact that <math id="A7.SS1.SSS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left&lt;\bm{b}\bm{b}^{\top}\right&gt;=\sigma^{2}L^{-2}\alpha^{-1}\bm{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><mrow><mi>𝒃</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left&lt;\bm{b}\bm{b}^{\top}\right&gt;=\sigma^{2}L^{-2}\alpha^{-1}\bm{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> we have the following loss function</p>
<table id="A7.EGx114" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E122"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E122.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\left|\bm{\Lambda}^{1/2}\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\bm{A}^{\ell}\bar{\bm{\beta}}\right|^{2}\right&gt;+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{L^{2}\alpha}\sum_{\ell\ell^{\prime}}\gamma^{\ell}\gamma^{\ell^{\prime}}\text{tr}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\prod_{k=\ell+1}^{L}\bm{A}^{k}\right)\bm{\Lambda}\left(\prod_{k=\ell^{\prime}+1}^{L}\bm{A}^{k}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>⟨</mo><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝚲</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>γ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{D}\left&lt;\left|\bm{\Lambda}^{1/2}\prod_{\ell=1}^{L}\bm{A}^{\ell}\bar{\bm{\beta}}\right|^{2}\right&gt;+\frac{\sigma^{2}}{L^{2}\alpha}\sum_{\ell\ell^{\prime}}\gamma^{\ell}\gamma^{\ell^{\prime}}\text{tr}\bm{\Lambda}\left(\prod_{k=\ell+1}^{L}\bm{A}^{k}\right)\bm{\Lambda}\left(\prod_{k=\ell^{\prime}+1}^{L}\bm{A}^{k}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(122)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.2 </span>Decoupling Weights in Attention Layers</h3>

<div id="A7.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We note that for the <span id="A7.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ISO</span> and <span id="A7.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RRS</span> settings, we can exploit similar symmetry arguments as in <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Gradient Flow in Deep Models ‣ Appendix C Isotropic (ISO) Setting Theory ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> and <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Randomly Rotated and Structured Covariance (RRS) Setting ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> to argue that the gradient updates for <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{x},\bm{W}_{k},\bm{W}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{x},\bm{W}_{k},\bm{W}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> are isotropic and that <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> gets an update in the <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{w}_{o}\bm{w}_{y}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒘</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{w}_{o}\bm{w}_{y}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> direction. The gradient flow can be expressed in terms of the original gradients on <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\Gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\Gamma}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A7.EGx115" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E123.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\partial_{t}\bm{W}_{i}=-\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}\cdot\frac{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}{\partial\bm{W}_{i}}\ ,\ i\in\{x,k,q,v,o,y\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>𝚪</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>o</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\partial_{t}\bm{W}_{i}=-\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}\cdot\frac{\partial\bm{\Gamma}}{\partial\bm{W}_{i}}\ ,\ i\in\{x,k,q,v,o,y\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(123)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">As before, under the assumption of small initial conditions, we can reduce the loss to a collection of ODEs on scalars representing the scale of each weight matrix</p>
<table id="A7.EGx116" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(w_{o},w_{v},w_{q},w_{k},w_{x},w_{y})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(w_{o},w_{v},w_{q},w_{k},w_{x},w_{y})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E124.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\bm{\Lambda}\left[\bm{I}-w_{o}w_{y}\left(\bm{I}-\left[1-L^{-1}w_{v}w_{k}w_{q}(w_{x})^{2}\bm{\Lambda}\right]^{L}\right)\right]^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\bm{\Lambda}\left[\bm{I}-w_{o}w_{y}\left(\bm{I}-\left[1-L^{-1}w_{v}w_{k}w_{q}(w_{x})^{2}\bm{\Lambda}\right]^{L}\right)\right]^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(124)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Gradient flow dynamics on this loss function can reproduce the dynamics of the decoupled self attention model. Under the further assumption that <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{o}=w_{y}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>o</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{o}=w_{y}=1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can simplify the loss further to</p>
<table id="A7.EGx117" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E125.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(w_{v},w_{q},w_{k},w_{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(w_{v},w_{q},w_{k},w_{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E125.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\bm{\Lambda}\left[\bm{I}-L^{-1}w_{v}w_{k}w_{q}(w_{x})^{2}\bm{\Lambda}\right]^{2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\bm{\Lambda}\left[\bm{I}-L^{-1}w_{v}w_{k}w_{q}(w_{x})^{2}\bm{\Lambda}\right]^{2L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(125)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">We note that <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> will be updated twice as quickly as the other weights under gradient flow. To achieve balance, we can initialize it to have <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{x}(0)=\sqrt{2}w_{k}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{x}(0)=\sqrt{2}w_{k}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> and have <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{q}(0)=w_{k}(0)=w_{v}(0)=\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{q}(0)=w_{k}(0)=w_{v}(0)=\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. In this case, the loss can be further reduced to a function of a single variable</p>
<table id="A7.EGx118" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E126.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(w_{v},w_{q},w_{k},w_{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>v</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(w_{v},w_{q},w_{k},w_{x})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E126.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\bm{\Lambda}\left[\bm{I}-L^{-1}w(t)^{5}\bm{\Lambda}\right]^{2L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>tr</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝛀</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>5</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚲</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{tr}\ \bm{\Omega}\bm{\Lambda}\left[\bm{I}-L^{-1}w(t)^{5}\bm{\Lambda}\right]^{2L}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(126)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Under source and capacity assumptions, this will generate the following dynamics at large depth <math id="A7.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="A7.EGx119" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w(t)=t^{\frac{5}{5\beta+2}}\implies\mathcal{L}\sim t^{-\frac{5\beta}{5\beta+2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">⟹</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w(t)=t^{\frac{5}{5\beta+2}}\implies\mathcal{L}\sim t^{-\frac{5\beta}{5\beta+2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(127)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<figure id="A7.F9" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:41%;"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.01098v1/SOFTMAXMLP_T20000_lr0p0005_loss_vs_t.svg" id="A7.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:165/123;" width="165" height="123"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Softmax attention model with MLP Blocks on the residual stream also benefit from increasing the depth.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">G.3 </span>Softmax Attention</h3>

<div id="A7.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We also provide numerical experiments with non-recurrent softmax attention, decoupled layers, and Adam. In this context we use CompleteP scaling for the learning rate <math id="A7.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Theta_{L}(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mi>L</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Theta_{L}(1)</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dey et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. The results are provided in Figure <a href="#S5.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 5.3 Nonlinear (Softmax) Attention ‣ 5 More Realistic Self Attention Models ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> (c).</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Supplementing this figure is an equivalent figure for a non-recurrent architecture with alternating softmax attention and MLP with GELU activation, given by Figure <a href="#A7.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ G.2 Decoupling Weights in Attention Layers ‣ Appendix G Enhancing Realism of the Model ‣ Theory of Scaling Laws for In-Context Regression: Depth, Width, Context and Time" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
